{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-49331","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-94165","marks":["code"],"text":"TRVM-HOLDOUT-OBSERVATION-v1"},{"id":"spn-94166","text":" — the neutral observation grammar"}]},{"id":"blk-49332","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94167","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status: PROCEDURAL, not normative."},{"id":"spn-94168","text":" This is the document format an implementation emits after applying a challenge recipe. It is the boundary between an implementation and the scorer."}]},{"id":"blk-49333","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94169","text":"Published "},{"id":"spn-94170","marks":["bold"],"text":"before"},{"id":"spn-94171","text":" any challenge is revealed. See "},{"id":"spn-94172","marks":["code"],"text":"HOLDOUT-RECIPE-v1.md"},{"id":"spn-94173","text":" §1."}]},{"id":"blk-49334","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-94174","text":"1. Why the boundary is a document"}]},{"id":"blk-49335","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94175","text":"Until P4.6 the scorer and the JavaScript implementation shared a process. The pure scoring function knew only the predicate operators, but the executable path was always"}]},{"id":"blk-49336","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"score(challenge, observeJS(challenge))"},{"id":"blk-49337","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94176","text":"so there was no way for anything other than JavaScript to be scored, and the claim "},{"id":"spn-94177","marks":["italic"],"text":"the scorer knows eight operators and no TRVM"},{"id":"spn-94178","text":" was true of a function and false of the program. A second implementation's observations had nowhere to enter."}]},{"id":"blk-49338","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94179","text":"A "},{"id":"spn-94180","marks":["bold"],"text":"document"},{"id":"spn-94181","text":" fixes that: each implementation writes one, the scorer reads them, and the scorer imports no protocol code. What the scorer cannot load, it cannot silently agree with."}]},{"id":"blk-49339","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-94182","text":"2. The envelope"}]},{"id":"blk-49340","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"type\": \"TRVM-HOLDOUT-OBSERVATION-v1\",\n  \"implementation\": \"javascript\",\n  \"spec_release_id\": \"srel-<64 hex>\",\n  \"observations\": { \"H0\": { … }, \"H1\": { … } }\n}"},{"head":[{"id":"blk-49342","spans":[{"id":"spn-94183","text":"field"}]},{"id":"blk-49343","spans":[{"id":"spn-94184","text":"meaning"}]}],"id":"blk-49341","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-49344","spans":[{"id":"spn-94185","marks":["code"],"text":"type"}]},{"id":"blk-49345","spans":[{"id":"spn-94186","text":"exactly this string; anything else is refused"}]}],[{"id":"blk-49346","spans":[{"id":"spn-94187","marks":["code"],"text":"implementation"}]},{"id":"blk-49347","spans":[{"id":"spn-94188","text":"free-form label naming the producer, e.g. "},{"id":"spn-94189","marks":["code"],"text":"javascript"},{"id":"spn-94190","text":", "},{"id":"spn-94191","marks":["code"],"text":"go"}]}],[{"id":"blk-49348","spans":[{"id":"spn-94192","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_release_id"}]},{"id":"blk-49349","spans":[{"id":"spn-94193","text":"the release this run was written against — see the contract §2"}]}],[{"id":"blk-49350","spans":[{"id":"spn-94194","marks":["code"],"text":"observations"}]},{"id":"blk-49351","spans":[{"id":"spn-94195","text":"one entry per challenge, keyed by the challenge "},{"id":"spn-94196","marks":["code"],"text":"id"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-49352","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94197","text":"Two observation documents are only comparable when their "},{"id":"spn-94198","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_release_id"},{"id":"spn-94199","text":" agree. A scorer that finds them different "},{"id":"spn-94200","marks":["bold"],"text":"reports it and refuses"},{"id":"spn-94201","text":", because comparing two implementations of two different specifications measures nothing."}]},{"id":"blk-49353","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-94202","text":"3. One observation"}]},{"id":"blk-49354","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94203","text":"Every member is optional. "},{"id":"spn-94204","marks":["bold"],"text":"A member that the recipe did not produce is ABSENT, never `null` and never a zero value"},{"id":"spn-94205","text":" — an observation asserting "},{"id":"spn-94206","marks":["code"],"text":"\"verdict\": null"},{"id":"spn-94207","text":" claims the checker returned nothing, which is a different fact from not having been asked."}]},{"id":"blk-49355","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"baseline\":    { \"<node>\": { … }, \"leaf\": { … } },\n  \"candidate\":   { \"<node>\": { … }, \"leaf\": { … } },\n  \"refusal_set\": [\"nest-policy-weakened\"],\n  \"resolve\":     { \"outcome\": \"non-canonical-wire\" }\n}"},{"id":"blk-49356","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94208","marks":["code"],"text":"baseline"},{"id":"spn-94209","text":" is the fixture as the corpus holds it. "},{"id":"spn-94210","marks":["code"],"text":"candidate"},{"id":"spn-94211","text":" is what the recipe produced. A recipe of "},{"id":"spn-94212","marks":["code"],"text":"IDENTITY"},{"id":"spn-94213","text":" still yields a "},{"id":"spn-94214","marks":["code"],"text":"candidate"},{"id":"spn-94215","text":" — the same object, verified."}]},{"id":"blk-49357","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-94216","text":"3.1 A node record"}]},{"id":"blk-49358","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"artifact_root\":         \"root-<64 hex>\",\n  \"nested_claim_sem_id\":   \"nclaim-<64 hex>\",\n  \"verified_claim_sem_id\": \"vclaim-<64 hex>\",\n  \"verdict\":               \"VERIFIED\",\n  \"structure\": {\n    \"edges\": 4,\n    \"unique_artifacts\": 3,\n    \"max_depth_below\": 2,\n    \"bytes_if_inlined\": 0,\n    \"unique_bytes\": 0,\n    \"films_below_by_edge_multiplicity\": 266,\n    \"films_below_distinct\": 138,\n    \"cases_below_by_edge_multiplicity\": 144,\n    \"cases_below_distinct\": 80,\n    \"structure_sem_id\": \"nstruct-<64 hex>\"\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-49359","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94217","text":"Node names are the frozen DAG's: "},{"id":"spn-94218","marks":["code"],"text":"A"},{"id":"spn-94219","text":", "},{"id":"spn-94220","marks":["code"],"text":"B"},{"id":"spn-94221","text":", "},{"id":"spn-94222","marks":["code"],"text":"C1"},{"id":"spn-94223","text":", "},{"id":"spn-94224","marks":["code"],"text":"C2"},{"id":"spn-94225","text":", "},{"id":"spn-94226","marks":["code"],"text":"D"},{"id":"spn-94227","text":", plus "},{"id":"spn-94228","marks":["code"],"text":"leaf"},{"id":"spn-94229","text":" for a leaf fixture. "},{"id":"spn-94230","marks":["code"],"text":"verdict"},{"id":"spn-94231","text":" is one of "},{"id":"spn-94232","marks":["code"],"text":"VERIFIED"},{"id":"spn-94233","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-94234","marks":["code"],"text":"REFUSED"},{"id":"spn-94235","text":" and appears only on the node that was actually verified."}]},{"id":"blk-49360","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94236","marks":["code"],"text":"structure"},{"id":"spn-94237","text":" is reported "},{"id":"spn-94238","marks":["bold"],"text":"verbatim as the artifact carries it"},{"id":"spn-94239","text":". An implementation does not recompute, round, reorder or omit members here; the point of the plane is that two implementations either derived the same structural facts or did not."}]},{"id":"blk-49361","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-94240","text":"3.2 "},{"id":"spn-94241","marks":["code"],"text":"refusal_set"}]},{"id":"blk-49362","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"\"refusal_set\": [\"nest-citation-cross-wired\", \"nest-structure-mismatch\"]"},{"id":"blk-49363","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94242","text":"A "},{"id":"spn-94243","marks":["bold"],"text":"sorted array of distinct refusal codes"},{"id":"spn-94244","text":", and the sortedness is what makes byte equality the same thing as set equality. A verification that refused nothing emits "},{"id":"spn-94245","marks":["code"],"text":"[]"},{"id":"spn-94246","text":". A verification that did not happen omits the member entirely — those are different observations and a predicate can tell them apart."}]},{"id":"blk-49364","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-94247","text":"3.3 "},{"id":"spn-94248","marks":["code"],"text":"resolve"}]},{"id":"blk-49365","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"\"resolve\": { \"outcome\": \"non-canonical-wire\" }"},{"id":"blk-49366","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94249","text":"Present only for a challenge that served octets under an address. "},{"id":"spn-94250","marks":["code"],"text":"outcome"},{"id":"spn-94251","text":" is the observable resolution outcome from "},{"id":"spn-94252","marks":["code"],"text":"TRVM-PROOF-WIRE-v1.md"},{"id":"spn-94253","text":" §3.3 — the "},{"id":"spn-94254","marks":["italic"],"text":"outcome"},{"id":"spn-94255","text":", not the internal stage at which a strict parser happened to notice, per §3.6."}]},{"id":"blk-49367","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-94256","text":"4. How a predicate path resolves"}]},{"id":"blk-49368","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94257","text":"Exactly one root per operator, stated here, with "},{"id":"spn-94258","marks":["bold"],"text":"no fallback chain"},{"id":"spn-94259","text":". An implementation of the scorer that tries one root and then another will disagree with this document on some input, and the disagreement will look like a protocol finding."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-49370","spans":[{"id":"spn-94260","text":"op"}]},{"id":"blk-49371","spans":[{"id":"spn-94261","marks":["code"],"text":"path"},{"id":"spn-94262","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-94263","marks":["code"],"text":"left"},{"id":"spn-94264","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-94265","marks":["code"],"text":"right"},{"id":"spn-94266","text":" resolve against"}]}],"id":"blk-49369","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-49372","spans":[{"id":"spn-94267","marks":["code"],"text":"HOLDS"},{"id":"spn-94268","text":", "},{"id":"spn-94269","marks":["code"],"text":"MOVES"}]},{"id":"blk-49373","spans":[{"id":"spn-94270","marks":["code"],"text":"baseline"},{"id":"spn-94271","text":" "},{"id":"spn-94272","marks":["bold"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-94273","text":" "},{"id":"spn-94274","marks":["code"],"text":"candidate"}]}],[{"id":"blk-49374","spans":[{"id":"spn-94275","marks":["code"],"text":"EQ"},{"id":"spn-94276","text":", "},{"id":"spn-94277","marks":["code"],"text":"NEQ"}]},{"id":"blk-49375","spans":[{"id":"spn-94278","text":"the observation root"}]}],[{"id":"blk-49376","spans":[{"id":"spn-94279","marks":["code"],"text":"VERDICT_EQ"}]},{"id":"blk-49377","spans":[{"id":"spn-94280","marks":["code"],"text":"candidate"}]}],[{"id":"blk-49378","spans":[{"id":"spn-94281","marks":["code"],"text":"OUTCOME_EQ"}]},{"id":"blk-49379","spans":[{"id":"spn-94282","text":"the observation root"}]}],[{"id":"blk-49380","spans":[{"id":"spn-94283","marks":["code"],"text":"REFUSAL_SET_EQ"}]},{"id":"blk-49381","spans":[{"id":"spn-94284","text":"no path; reads "},{"id":"spn-94285","marks":["code"],"text":"refusal_set"}]}],[{"id":"blk-49382","spans":[{"id":"spn-94286","marks":["code"],"text":"LT"}]},{"id":"blk-49383","spans":[{"id":"spn-94287","text":"the observation root"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-49384","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94288","text":"So "},{"id":"spn-94289","marks":["code"],"text":"MOVES"},{"id":"spn-94290","text":" of "},{"id":"spn-94291","marks":["code"],"text":"D.artifact_root"},{"id":"spn-94292","text":" reads "},{"id":"spn-94293","marks":["code"],"text":"baseline.D.artifact_root"},{"id":"spn-94294","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-94295","marks":["code"],"text":"candidate.D.artifact_root"},{"id":"spn-94296","text":", while "},{"id":"spn-94297","marks":["code"],"text":"EQ"},{"id":"spn-94298","text":" of "},{"id":"spn-94299","marks":["code"],"text":"candidate.C2.structure.edges"},{"id":"spn-94300","text":" must say "},{"id":"spn-94301","marks":["code"],"text":"candidate."},{"id":"spn-94302","text":" out loud."}]},{"id":"blk-49385","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94303","text":"A path that resolves to "},{"id":"spn-94304","marks":["bold"],"text":"absent on either side"},{"id":"spn-94305","text":" is not a pass and not a fail: it is "},{"id":"spn-94306","marks":["code"],"text":"UNRESOLVED"},{"id":"spn-94307","text":", and any unresolved predicate makes the whole scoring run fail. A missing observation scoring as a quiet zero is the failure mode this rule exists to prevent."}]},{"id":"blk-49386","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-94308","text":"5. Comparison rules"}]},{"id":"blk-49387","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49389","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94309","text":"Values compare by their "},{"id":"spn-94310","marks":["bold"],"text":"canonical JSON encoding"},{"id":"spn-94311","text":" (RFC 8785), so member order in a "},{"id":"spn-94312","marks":["code"],"text":"structure"}]}],"id":"blk-49388","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-49390","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94313","text":"record never decides a predicate."}]},{"id":"blk-49391","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49393","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94314","text":"Numbers compare as numbers. "},{"id":"spn-94315","marks":["code"],"text":"LT"},{"id":"spn-94316","text":" requires both sides to be numbers; a non-number is "},{"id":"spn-94317","marks":["code"],"text":"UNRESOLVED"},{"id":"spn-94318","text":","}]}],"id":"blk-49392","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-49394","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94319","text":"not "},{"id":"spn-94320","marks":["code"],"text":"false"},{"id":"spn-94321","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-49395","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-49397","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94322","text":"Strings compare by code points, as octets of their canonical encoding."}]}],"id":"blk-49396","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-49398","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-94323","text":"6. The scorer, and why it lives here"}]},{"id":"blk-49399","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"experiment/holdout_score_core.mjs   predicates + observations → results   imports NO protocol code\nexperiment/holdout_runner.mjs       adapters (as DATA) → runs, then compares observations\nexperiment/holdout_schema.mjs       this schema, executed\n<impl>_holdout_adapter              implementation → observations         imports the implementation"},{"id":"blk-49400","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94324","text":"The first three are "},{"id":"spn-94325","marks":["bold"],"text":"in the specification package"},{"id":"spn-94326","text":", not beside the implementation, and that is deliberate. They are inside "},{"id":"spn-94327","marks":["code"],"text":"experiment_digest"},{"id":"spn-94328","text":", therefore inside "},{"id":"spn-94329","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_release_id"},{"id":"spn-94330","text":", so "},{"id":"spn-94331","marks":["bold"],"text":"editing one byte of the scorer moves the release identity and reddens the pinned run."}]},{"id":"blk-49401","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94332","text":"The reason is a measured one. When the scorer lived outside every digest, inserting"}]},{"id":"blk-49402","kind":"code","language":"js","text":"if (entry.id.startsWith(\"H\")) { pass = true; continue; }"},{"id":"blk-49403","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94333","text":"left the synthetic fixture at 19/19 (its cases are not "},{"id":"spn-94334","marks":["code"],"text":"H*"},{"id":"spn-94335","text":"), the real holdout at 25/25, the release passing with an unchanged identity, and the pinned run passing. A synthetic fixture proves that one set of scorer behaviours works; it cannot prove the scorer later applied to the secret cases is the same scorer. "},{"id":"spn-94336","marks":["bold"],"text":"The instrument has to be content-bound"},{"id":"spn-94337","text":", exactly as the evidence and the subjects are."}]},{"id":"blk-49404","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94338","text":"Adapters are "},{"id":"spn-94339","marks":["bold"],"text":"data"},{"id":"spn-94340","text":", not source. The runner takes an adapter list — command plus the digest of that implementation's own package — and verifies the digest before executing it. Registering a second implementation changes the "},{"id":"spn-94341","marks":["italic"],"text":"run"},{"id":"spn-94342","text":", never the instrument."}]},{"id":"blk-49405","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-94343","text":"6.1 The boundary is executed"}]},{"id":"blk-49406","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94344","text":"Every observation document is validated against "},{"id":"spn-94345","marks":["code"],"text":"holdout-observation-v1.schema.json"},{"id":"spn-94346","text":", and every challenge against "},{"id":"spn-94347","marks":["code"],"text":"holdout-recipe-v1.schema.json"},{"id":"spn-94348","text":", "},{"id":"spn-94349","marks":["bold"],"text":"before scoring"},{"id":"spn-94350","text":". An unknown member, a malformed root, a duplicated or unsorted refusal code, a wrong type, a wrong envelope or a "},{"id":"spn-94351","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_release_id"},{"id":"spn-94352","text":" that is not the run's release is "},{"id":"spn-94353","marks":["bold"],"text":"refused"},{"id":"spn-94354","text":", not scored. A schema that documents a boundary nobody executes is prose."}]},{"id":"blk-49407","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94355","marks":["code"],"text":"experiment/fixtures/"},{"id":"spn-94356","text":" carries synthetic challenges and observations containing no TRVM value at all, whose declared result includes the "},{"id":"spn-94357","marks":["bold"],"text":"failing arm of every operator"},{"id":"spn-94358","text":", an "},{"id":"spn-94359","marks":["bold"],"text":"unresolved arm"},{"id":"spn-94360","text":", and a set of documents that must be "},{"id":"spn-94361","marks":["bold"],"text":"refused outright"},{"id":"spn-94362","text":", one per boundary rule. A fixture whose every case is accepted cannot tell a validator from a pass-through."}]},{"id":"blk-49408","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-94363","text":"6.2 Conformance and interoperability are different questions"}]},{"id":"blk-49409","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94364","marks":["code"],"text":"HOLDOUT-HARNESS"},{"id":"spn-94365","text":" asks whether each implementation satisfied the frozen predicates. One implementation may legitimately pass it."}]},{"id":"blk-49410","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94366","marks":["code"],"text":"HOLDOUT-INTEROP"},{"id":"spn-94367","text":" asks whether two frozen implementations "},{"id":"spn-94368","marks":["bold"],"text":"saw the same thing"},{"id":"spn-94369","text":", and it is decided by deep-comparing the normalized observation documents — every member, not only what the predicates happen to read. With fewer than two frozen implementations it reports "},{"id":"spn-94370","marks":["bold"],"text":"NOT MEASURED"},{"id":"spn-94371","text":" and never PASS."}]},{"id":"blk-49411","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94372","text":"Comparing predicate "},{"id":"spn-94373","marks":["italic"],"text":"results"},{"id":"spn-94374","text":" is not enough: mutating one "},{"id":"spn-94375","marks":["code"],"text":"artifact_root"},{"id":"spn-94376","text":" that no frozen predicate reads leaves both implementations scoring identically while their observations plainly disagree."}]},{"id":"blk-49412","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94377","text":"The core scorer assigns "},{"id":"spn-94378","marks":["bold"],"text":"no blame"},{"id":"spn-94379","text":". A disagreement is an "},{"id":"spn-94380","marks":["code"],"text":"UNCLASSIFIED_FINDING"},{"id":"spn-94381","text":" for a human to categorise, and it "},{"id":"spn-94382","marks":["bold"],"text":"blocks completion"},{"id":"spn-94383","text":" rather than printing underneath a PASS."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierawsi67jf3dizn7f25idbehovdzcikxfxmzc7xylpvbzpb7bkth4jq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}